WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.897
A four billion parameter model that beats all eight of its parents.

00:00:03.897 --> 00:00:04.759
That's the claim.

00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:07.408
But the merge was chosen on these same questions.

00:00:09.665 --> 00:00:10.630
Hi, I'm Ozias!

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.202
Baphomet one point one was made without training.

00:00:13.202 --> 00:00:15.775
Here is the search, and the held-out test.

00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:20.309
Every parent is the same Qwen base plus a change.

00:00:20.309 --> 00:00:23.918
Draw each change as an arrow, and the arrow's tip is the parent.

00:00:24.338 --> 00:00:27.772
The search starts from each parent alone, from their plain average,

00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:29.020
and from random mixes.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.566
Then it settles on one weight per parent.

00:00:31.566 --> 00:00:33.957
The Qwen three point eight distill gets the most.

00:00:34.377 --> 00:00:38.030
Add the scaled arrows head to tail and you land on the merge.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.997
Eight numbers, the same for every layer.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.484
The search is EvoGM.

00:00:43.484 --> 00:00:47.159
Seed a population: the parents, their average, random mixes.

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:50.085
Score each candidate on a hundred and ten questions.

00:00:50.085 --> 00:00:53.173
An answer cut off at the token cap counts as wrong.

00:00:53.573 --> 00:00:54.154
Split them.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.898
The top thirty percent are winners.

00:00:56.298 --> 00:01:01.247
A small network learns to move losers toward winners, and proposes the next candidates.

00:01:01.647 --> 00:01:03.861
Then the best mixes become the new parents.

00:01:05.408 --> 00:01:07.236
That loop, in the paper's own drawing.

00:01:08.758 --> 00:01:12.146
On those questions the merge scores seventy-six point four.

00:01:12.146 --> 00:01:14.405
Its best parent, sixty-eight point six.

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:19.511
The weights it found: point five nine on the Qwen three point eight distill.

00:01:19.891 --> 00:01:22.264
The five agent fine-tunes get almost nothing.

00:01:24.392 --> 00:01:25.583
Now the held-out test.

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:29.454
One point one gets a hundred and forty-three of a hundred and eighty.

00:01:29.874 --> 00:01:32.339
Against one point oh, they disagree on seventeen.

00:01:32.339 --> 00:01:34.495
Ten go one way, seven the other.

00:01:34.495 --> 00:01:36.035
A coin does that often.

00:01:37.442 --> 00:01:40.485
One point oh runs out of room on twenty-eight answers.

00:01:41.615 --> 00:01:45.726
One point one is cut off on eighteen and writes about half as much.

00:01:45.726 --> 00:01:48.662
Of the ten extra answers it finishes, seven are wrong.

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:54.472
The improvements in benchmark scores remained marginal and not significant.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.686
The search found a merge that thinks shorter.

00:01:58.686 --> 00:02:02.012
Whether it beats its parents on fresh questions was never tested.

00:02:04.692 --> 00:02:07.865
Eight weights, a small fitness set, three items of difference.

00:02:07.865 --> 00:02:08.817
Thanks for watching!

00:02:09.292 --> 00:02:11.426
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:11.426 --> 00:02:12.036
I'm Ozias.

00:02:12.036 --> 00:02:12.341
Bye!
